WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.227 --> 00:00:02.644
(soft music)

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:10.063
- [Hudda] I vividly remember
the Civil War in Somalia.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.090
Of course there was fear there.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.640
It was not a safe place for us.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.140
And that's the reason why
we left our own country.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.800
- [Minnie] When Hudda landed in the U.S.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.170
she had no idea that her
neighbors would be afraid of her.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.750
- I have been told that
there are certain customs

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.320
in the Somali culture that
I'm not supposed to transgress

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.840
and I don't know what they are.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.680
- I think we need to know
more about their religion,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.840
where they're coming from
because I was understood

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.240
you never ever shake hands.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.750
- People are genuinely
interested in getting to know us

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.290
that's why they're coming
to Dine and Dialogue

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.060
in large numbers.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.793
We wanna help them overcome
the fear of unknown.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.510
My name is Hudda Ibrahim and
I started Dine and Dialogue

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.283
and I'm a refugee from Somalia.

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:02.290
(dramatic music)

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.990
- My name is Minnie Driver.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.710
I am an actress, a singer
and I am an immigrant.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.970
I believe nothing is more
American than its immigrants.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.580
So I'm teaming up with
Great Big Story to celebrate

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:18.313
those that have come
here and left their mark.

00:01:23.502 --> 00:01:25.919
(soft music)

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.600
- [Hudda] I was 19 years old
when I came to Minnesota.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.630
It was a long journey.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.310
- [Minnie] During the Somali Civil War

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.670
large numbers of Somalis
relocated to Minnesota.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.630
Today the state has the largest population

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:41.303
of Somalis in North America.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.270
But the influx of Somali refugees

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.120
has created tension in the community.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.520
- Moving into this central
Minnesota community

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.210
people are curious about our culture

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.150
and who we are and where we came from.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.160
Of course we do have challenges.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.180
I am Muslim, I am black, I am a refugee,

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.060
but I'm also Somali American.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.957
So instead of being angry and complaining

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.840
my husband and I turned
it to the other side

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.580
and said we should do
something about this.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.920
- [Minnie] So Hudda and her husband

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.400
started Dine and Dialogue, a
bi-monthly dinner gathering

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.680
where the St. Cloud community

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.820
can meet their Somali neighbors.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.370
- People were afraid to ask questions

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.920
that they thought were
inappropriate or offensive.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.130
And when individuals usually
come to those dinners

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.080
we say, ask us any burning
questions that you might have.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.720
Questions like, what is the
significance of the hijab?

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.060
Why do Muslims pray five times a day?

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.060
So instead of assuming, I
want people to be open minded.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.770
The first Dine and Dialogue
we didn't know who was coming,

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:46.520
we just sent an open invitation to all.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.140
My husband and I couldn't believe

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.460
when we saw 50 registration

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.910
and we were like we need to make sure

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:54.323
that we have enough food
for these people coming.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.800
- [Minnie] Hudda helps
cook a massive Somali meal

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.120
for all who attend.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.640
And she attributes some
of her program's success

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.500
to the meals themselves.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.344
- Food is one of the main contributors

00:03:06.344 --> 00:03:08.770
really bringing people together.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.000
There were a lot of people who told me

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.350
that they never had any Somali food before

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.910
and that they love the sambusa.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:21.100
We make sure that the
sambusas are ready to fry.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.520
When we make rice we make sure
that we have the right meat,

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.650
we have goat meat.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:28.250
We make sure that we
have chicken and beef,

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.110
veggie and Somali tea.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:34.270
So do not leave this room
today without knowing someone,

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.982
so get to know your
neighbors, ask questions,

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:39.110
thank you very much.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.890
- I feel that I want to be compassionate,

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.290
I feel that I want to
care, I'm just afraid

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.090
that I'm gonna do something
that's gonna offend somebody.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:49.820
- Once you're open to the idea
of somebody being different

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.780
then there's more common than
there is actually differences.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.199
- But if you are afraid to make a mistake

00:03:55.199 --> 00:03:57.925
and they're afraid to make a mistake,

00:03:57.925 --> 00:04:00.425
then there is a disconnection.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.230
- [Minnie] Today she continues to host

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.520
this open forum every other month

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.093
and hopes to expand
into other communities.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.490
- I'm hoping to spread Dine and Dialogue

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.833
throughout Minnesota.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:18.810
I devoted my life to build a
better community for all of us.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.530
And I want people to know
that we're proud Americans,

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:26.830
we're taxpayers, we're
contributing to the economy

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.172
and that we're here to stay.

00:04:29.172 --> 00:04:31.755
(upbeat music)

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:36.188
(bell ringing)

